// ANCHOR: new
$ sspur new web-app notes
created notes from the web-app template

  cd notes
  sspur run              # then open http://127.0.0.1:8080
  sspur run tests/run.ssp

README.md has the rest: configuration, debugging, backups and deploying.
// ANCHOR_END: new
$ cd notes
// ANCHOR: test
$ sspur test
5 passed, 0 failed
$ sspur test tests/storage.ssp
8 passed, 0 failed
$ sspur run tests/e2e.ssp
e2e passed (server native): 350 notes, 800 requests
...
// ANCHOR_END: test
// ANCHOR: serve
$ NOTES_PORT=8080 NOTES_SECRET=use-openssl-rand-base64-48-for-a-real-one sspur run &
info: {"event":"started","mode":"dev","db":"notes.db","migrations":4}
info: listening on http://127.0.0.1:8080
// ANCHOR_END: serve
// ANCHOR: curl
$ curl -s -w ' %{http_code}\n' localhost:8080/api/health
{"status":"ok","db":true} 200
$ curl -s -w ' %{http_code}\n' localhost:8080/api/signup -d '{"email":"ada","password":"correct horse battery"}'
{"error":"invalid request","detail":"body.email: must satisfy models.email_ok(_)"} 400
$ curl -s -w ' %{http_code}\n' localhost:8080/api/signup -d '{"email":"ada@example.com","password":"password123"}'
{"error":{"tag":"Invalid","field":"password","why":"the password is too easy to guess"}} 400
$ curl -s -w ' %{http_code}\n' localhost:8080/api/notes
{"error":"Unauthorized"} 401
// ANCHOR_END: curl
